Description: Breeze widget style and window decoration with Soft, Glass and Aurora looks
 Breeze NG is a fork of KDE's Breeze widget style and window decoration with
 three looks: Soft (surfaces told apart by tone, no separator lines), Glass
 (translucent windows and menus blurred by the compositor) and Aurora (the
 whole window as frosted glass). It installs under /opt/ng/breeze-ng, next to
 the stock Breeze, which stays untouched, with links to its plugins in Qt's
 plugin folder.
 .
 It also brings Plasma styles in the same looks, colour schemes, global themes
 and Aurora for Kirigami (Qt Quick) applications.
 .
 After installing, pick a "Breeze NG" global theme in System Settings >
 Colours & Themes > Global Theme. Applications already open keep their old
 style until restarted; Kirigami applications need a new login.
